<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumo Xi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kumo Xi, or Xi, were a nomadic people of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-river">Liao River</a> region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>, closely related to the Khitan and traced by Chinese sources to the Yuwen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>. They were subject in turn to the Turks, the Tang and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a>, and from the 10th century were absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Khitan Liao</a> state, where they formed a distinct part of its army and administration.</p></div>
